##  lessence fold regressions — one block per bug we actually hit.
##
##  The examples/ corpora are ~100 MB of real logs, gitignored, and live on one
##  machine. This file is the opposite: the smallest input that reproduces each
##  past defect, checked into git, asserted in milliseconds. A case earns its
##  place by having been a real bug — ##FROM is the receipt, and several were
##  confirmed by running the stored v0.4.1 binary and watching it get them wrong.
##
##  Block format, blank-line separated:
##    ##CASE <bead-or-commit> <expectation>
##    ##WHY  <what the case protects, one line>
##    ##FROM <where the shape came from>
##    <input lines>
##
##  Expectations:
##    groups=N     the lines must end up in exactly N groups
##    absent=<TOK> the first line's normalized form must NOT contain <TOK>
##    present=TEXT the first line's normalized form MUST contain TEXT
##
##  Lines are either from an Apache-2.0 licensed corpus, stock upstream product
##  text, or reproduce the SHAPE of a private corpus without its content.
##  Add a case whenever a fold bug is fixed — cheaper than re-deriving the
##  reproduction from a bead six months later.

##CASE lessence-8jb groups=1
##WHY a field value folds on its shape, not on how long it happens to be
##FROM argocd controller shape; the 25-char rule split these by name length
{"application":"redis-sentinel","level":"info","msg":"Update successful"}
{"application":"redis-sentinel-gitlab","level":"info","msg":"Update successful"}
{"application":"redis-sentinel-gitlab-prod","level":"info","msg":"Update successful"}
{"application":"redis-sentinel-gitlab-prod-eu","level":"info","msg":"Update successful"}

##CASE lessence-8jb groups=2
##WHY a bare word is shape-identical to a log level, so it must never fold
##FROM the guard that keeps error lines out of info groups
{"level":"info","msg":"reconcile finished"}
{"level":"error","msg":"reconcile finished"}

##CASE lessence-8jb groups=1
##WHY a JSON number folds whatever its digit count
##FROM argocd reconciliation shape; a latency crossing 100 ms used to split the group
{"msg":"Reconciliation completed","diff_ms":4,"git_ms":4}
{"msg":"Reconciliation completed","diff_ms":82,"git_ms":82}
{"msg":"Reconciliation completed","diff_ms":123,"git_ms":123}
{"msg":"Reconciliation completed","diff_ms":4567,"git_ms":4567}

##CASE lessence-8jb present=application
##WHY a JSON key keeps its name in the template; only the value folds
##FROM the one-byte colon lookahead in QuotedStringDetector
{"application":"redis-sentinel-gitlab","level":"info","msg":"Update successful"}

##CASE lessence-fo2 groups=1
##WHY a record past the similarity token cap folds on the same basis as a short one
##FROM gitaly shape, ~1 KB; these used to land in one group each
